    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32193": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Postdoctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Postdoctoral Research Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07098P Position Title Postdoctoral Research Associate Functional Title Postdoc Department Chemistry Salary Range $55,000; Dependent on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 06/25/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 08/15/2026 Job Summary The Romiti Group in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of Texas at Dallas, has a postdoctoral position available in the area of catalytic methods development and complex biologically active molecule synthesis. We are seeking a highly motivated and independent scientist with a strong background in organic synthesis and is excited about organic chemistry, synthesis and catalysis, to join our research team. Complex molecule synthesis experience is required. The postdoc will develop high-impact and practical catalytic transformations, and creative, novel synthesis strategies for the concise and efficient preparation of bioactive complex natural products and analogs thereof. The postdoc will also serve as a mentor to junior graduate students. The candidate should have completed a Ph.D. within the last three years or soon to be completed in chemistry or a related discipline. Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D in a related field. Candidates who have successfully completed all requirements for the Ph.D. but whose degree has not yet been formally conferred may be eligible to begin employment provided they submit an official letter from the Registrar or Graduate School of the degree-granting institution certifying that all doctoral requirements have been satisfied and specifying the expected date of conferral. Appointment and continued employment are contingent upon formal conferral of the Ph.D. Preferred Education and Experience PhD in Chemistry or a related field Written and oral communication skills with a proven record of scientific accomplishment We are looking for an enthusiastic and ambitious scientist excited to work in a highly interactive and motivated research environment. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Plan, conduct, and direct a wide variety of experiments. Responsible for the evaluation and interpretation of research data. Conduct experiments using advanced equipment and applying complex techniques, methods and procedures. Develop research protocols and supervise graduate or undergraduate researchers. Prepare written reports and contribute to the writing of research articles. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work is conducted on site and in person. What we have to Offer: UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We offer an employee-friendly work environment with a comprehensive benefit package including: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Medical insurance – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability Retirement Plan Paid time off Paid Holidays About UT Dallas The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. UT Dallas is a place where members of the community are welcomed, treated fairly, and encouraged to their pursuit of excellence. UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Other Document Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32565": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Davidson Management Honors Program (JSOM)",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Program Manager, Davidson Management Honors Program (JSOM) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Program Manager, Davidson Management Honors Program (JSOM) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07213P Position Title Program Manager, Davidson Management Honors Program (JSOM) Functional Title Department Management Salary Range $56,000, DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The Program Manager serves as a key member of the Davidson Management Honors Program ( DMHP ) and is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, and assessment of programs and services that support student success, leadership development, engagement, recruitment, and community building. Reporting to the DMHP Director and working closely with the DMHP Associate Dean, this position plays an integral role in enhancing the undergraduate experience for approximately 2 50 high-achieving business honors students . The Program Manager serves as a primary point of contact for current and prospective students and collaborates with faculty, staff, alumni, and university partners to support a vibrant and engaged honors community. Responsibilities include student advising, leadership and mentoring programs, recruitment and admissions processes, student engagement initiatives, communications and marketing efforts, event planning, and program operations. The successful candidate will be passionate about student development and committed to creating meaningful experiences that foster connection, belonging, academic excellence, and professional growth. This position requires significant interaction with students, occasional travel, and evening and weekend commitments to support recruitment activities, student events, conferences, competitions, retreats, and experiential learning opportunities. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree. Three (3) years of related experience. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, Business, or a related field. Three to five years of experience in student affairs, academic advising, honors education, program administration, recruitment, student leadership, or related higher education programs. Experience developing and coordinating student programs and events. Experience supervising student employees or student leaders. Experience creating marketing materials using Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, or similar platforms. Experience managing budgets, purchasing, and financial transactions. Experience using CRM , student information, or related database systems. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSA’s) Strong interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills. Ability to advise, mentor, and support undergraduate students. Strong organizational, project management, and multitasking abilities. Ability to plan and execute programs, events, and engagement initiatives. Ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external partners. Strong problem-solving and customer service skills. Commitment to fostering a student-centered environment. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Student Advising and Success Serve as advisor for approximately 125 Davidson Management Honors Program students. Meet individually with students regularly regarding academic planning, program requirements, leadership development, professional goals, and overall student success. Connect students with campus resources and support services as needed. Track student participation and progress toward program requirements. Student Leadership Programs Coordinate the DMHP Peer Mentor Program, including selection, placement, supervision, and assessment of approximately 30 student Peer Mentors. Collaborate with the DMHP Director to develop and manage Peer Mentor groups, thoughtfully matching first-year students with upper-class mentors based on academic interests, career aspirations, extracurricular involvement, leadership experiences, and personal interests to foster meaningful relationships and support successful transitions into DMHP . Facilitate ongoing engagement, communication, and support within Peer Mentor groups throughout the academic year. Coordinate and supervise the DMHP CORE (Community, Outreach, Recruitment, and Engagement) Team, consisting of approximately 15 student leaders who support recruitment, community building, student engagement, and outreach efforts. Recruit, train, mentor, and provide leadership development opportunities for Peer Mentors and CORE Team members. Coach student leaders in planning and implementing recruitment activities, service projects, outreach efforts, and program events. Monitor the effectiveness of Peer mentoring and student leadership programs and recommend improvements to enhance student engagement and community building. Recruitment and Admissions Manage admissions workflow from application receipt to enrollment. Coordinate applicant interviews and participate in the interview and holistic review process in collaboration with the DMHP Director. Track admissions and enrollment data and prepare reports to support program decision-making. Develop admissions communications. Coordinate prospective and admitted student events and information sessions. Represent DMHP at university and Jindal School recruitment events. Support enrollment and yield efforts through outreach and engagement with prospective and admitted students. Build relationships with prospective students and families and communicate program opportunities and expectations. Community Building & Student Engagement Plan, coordinate, and execute social events, community service projects, and student engagement initiatives throughout the year. Maintain relationships with nonprofit and community partners. Promote a sense of community, belonging, and connection among DMHP students. Travel and Experiential Learning Support the planning and implementation of the annual domestic trip, including logistics, participant communications, travel preparations, and on-site coordination, while traveling with the DMHP Director and/or DMHP Associate Dean. Manage travel documentation, participant requirements, and compliance-related travel processes. Accompany students to conferences, case competitions, employer visits, and other experiential learning opportunities as needed. Serve as a university representative during student travel and support student participation in off-campus learning experiences. Marketing and Communications Manage DMHP Instagram and LinkedIn accounts. Create and implement social media content strategies. Develop recruitment and promotional content for marketing and outreach initiatives. Create digital and print marketing materials to support program communications and branding. Highlight student accomplishments and program successes. Program Operations and Administration Serve as departmental One Card holder. Coordinate and process purchases according to university policies. Process reimbursements, travel authorizations, and expense reports. Manage vendor contracts and payment requests. Coordinate event logistics, catering, transportation, and supplies. Maintain relationships with vendors and service providers. Assist with budget tracking and financial reporting. Support risk management and compliance requirements related to events, programs, and travel. Other Duties Perform other duties and special projects as assigned in support of the mission, goals, and learning outcomes of the Davidson Management Honors Program. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information About the Davidson Management Honors Program ( DMHP ) The Davidson Management Honors Program ( DMHP ) is one of the Naveen Jindal School of Management’s premier undergraduate programs, serving a highly engaged community of ambitious, high-achieving business students. Through leadership development, professional networking, employer engagement, community service, scholarship opportunities, domestic and international travel, and meaningful interaction with faculty, staff, alumni, and industry partners, DMHP provides students with a distinctive honors experience that extends beyond the classroom. At its core, DMHP is a relationship-driven community where students are known, supported, challenged, and encouraged throughout their undergraduate journey. Meaningful connections among students, faculty, staff, alumni, and employer partners are central to the program’s culture and contribute to an environment where students can thrive academically, professionally, and personally. DMHP is committed to fostering a culture of kindness, respect, professionalism, and student-centered service. Successful community members value collaboration, engagement, leadership, and lifelong learning, helping to create a supportive environment where students are empowered to reach their full potential. Through a combination of academic excellence, leadership opportunities, experiential learning, community engagement, and personalized support, DMHP provides a transformative undergraduate experience that prepares students to become successful business leaders and engaged members of their communities. Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person. What We Can Offer: UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits BCBS PPO Medical Insurance Options – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees AD&D Insurance Dental & Vision Plan Options Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Fertility Benefits Paid time off All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
