    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32077": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Research Scientist - DILLON / DENISCO Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Research Scientist - DILLON / DENISCO Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07066P Position Title Research Scientist - DILLON / DENISCO Lab Functional Title Research Associate - Post Doc (DILLON / DENISCO LAB) Department Biological Sciences Salary Range $62,232 - Dependent on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 06/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 08/03/2026 Job Summary The Dillon and De Nisco laboratories are looking to hire a co-mentored postdoctoral scholar to work on collaborative projects on improving antibiotic outcomes in urinary tract infection management. The Dillon lab seeks to decipher the basis for how antibiotic resistance evolves, specializing in research on high-priority MDR pathogens, antibiotic pharmacology, and host-pathogen interactions including murine models of infection. Our current focus is how we can modify the host microenvironment to improve antibiotic efficacies. The De Nisco lab is focused on understanding mechanisms of microbial pathogenesis, host response, and urinary microbiome structure and function contributing to recurrent urinary tract infection (rUTI) in postmenopausal women. A current major research focus of the De Nisco lab is the role of the urinary microenvironment in UTI susceptibility and treatment outcomes. We seek to understand how the female urinary tract is shaped by aging, hormonal status, and history of infection using metagenomics, advanced statistical models, and analytical biochemistry. This position will be co-mentored by two TT Faculty in two different laboratories. Minimum Education and Experience Ph.D in a related field. Candidates who have successfully completed all requirements for the Ph.D. but whose degree has not yet been formally conferred may be eligible to begin employment provided they submit an official letter from the Registrar or Graduate School of the degree-granting institution certifying that all doctoral requirements have been satisfied and specifying the expected date of conferral. Appointment and continued employment are contingent upon formal conferral of the Ph.D. Preferred Education and Experience The successful postdoctoral applicant should have a proven academic publication track record, including multiple first-authored publications in well-respected peer-reviewed journals, as well as excellent scientific, organizational, record-keeping, problem-solving skills. Candidates with expertise in host-microbe interactions related to bacterial infections, defining drug mechanisms of action, microbiome analysis, and exploring how host microenvironments impact treatment efficacies will be prioritized. The selected candidate will also be encouraged to explore new research areas and seek independent NIH or foundation funding as part of their own career development. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Work on collaborative projects on improving antibiotic outcomes in urinary tract infection management. The candidate will conduct independent research on both established and new projects in the Dillon and De Nisco lab. Defining the mechanistic basis for minocycline resistance in Acinetobacter baumannii in the Dillon lab. Characterizing host urinary microbiome changes in human clinical cohorts in the De Nisco lab. Decipher the basis for how antibiotic resistance evolves, specializing in research on high-priority MDR pathogens, antibiotic pharmacology, and host-pathogen interactions including murine models of infection. Physical Demands and Working Conditions laboratory environment Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid Time off Fertility Benefits About Us UT Dallas is a top public research university located in one of the nation’s fastest-growing metropolitan regions. Our seven schools offer more than 140 undergraduate and graduate programs, plus professional certificates and fast-track programs. Our student body is 31,000 strong, reflecting students from over 100 countries and a multiplicity of identities and experiences. UT Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Research Statement Other Document Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32528": {
      "title": "Program Specialist II",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Program Specialist II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Program Specialist II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07207P Position Title Program Specialist II Functional Title Recruitment Specialist Department Interdisciplinary Studies Salary Range $58,000 DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 08/25/2026 Posting Close Date 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The position is responsible for providing expertise to implement, develop, and evaluate enrollment initiatives, develop recruitment strategies, and assist the department of Interdisciplinary Studies with strategic implementation of recruitment activities by identifying strong recruitment approaches and developing outreach programs. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in a related field, with five years of experience working with students and programs in higher education, or related community programs; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree and three years experience in higher education recruitment; effective communication and leadership skills; ability to travel to partnering schools. Ability to develop and deliver presentations. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Ability to gather data, compile information, and prepare reports. Ability to develop, plan, and implement short- and long-range goals. Ability to plan, assess, and evaluate programs. Organizing and coordinating skills. Skill in the configuration and use of computerized database programs. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Participates in the development of student recruitment and retention plans, strategies, and written materials. • Visits middle schools, high schools, and colleges, speaks to groups and individual students, and meets with school counselors to promote outreach activities. • Serves as a liaison to develop partnerships between the university and local school systems throughout the state. • Creates a database of prospective and current students and/or potential degree candidates in the state. • Distributes resource materials for student recruitment and retention programs; develops mentorship programs; analyzes trends in recruitment and retention programs; develops strategies for program evaluation. • Develops operating goals and objectives for the unit; implements and administers methods and procedures to enhance operations, as appropriate to the unit. • Coordinates recruitment initiatives with Interdisciplinary Studies staff and faculty. • Evening availability may be required, as well as travel to on- and off-campus recruitment and admission events. • Responsible for transporting recruitment materials and supplies to and from events, including loading and unloading materials, and for the physical setup and breakdown of event equipment such as tables, awnings/canopies, displays, and carts containing recruitment supplies. • Performs miscellaneous job-related duties as assigned. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Some repetitive motion, walking, lifting heavy items up to 50lbs Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information A remote work schedule is not available for this position. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees PPO and DHMO Dental Insurance Plan – PPO plans include ortho benefits Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan – defined benefit plan offering lifetime annuity upon retirement Voluntary Retirement Plan Options – additional savings opportunities with Tax-Sheltered Annuity Plans and Deferred Compensation Plans Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid time off Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break Fertility Benefits All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. If you are looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team! Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Other Document Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32378": {
      "title": "Career Development Specialist (JSOM)",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Career Development Specialist (JSOM) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Career Development Specialist (JSOM) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07161P Position Title Career Development Specialist (JSOM) Functional Title Department Management Salary Range $55,000 Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 07/22/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Job Summary The Career Development Specialist ( CDS ) for the JSOM Career Management Center ( CMC ) plays a vital role in preparing undergraduate students for career success. This position provides personalized coaching in résumé development, networking, LinkedIn optimization, cover letter writing, mock interviews, and internship search strategies. The CDS will meet with students individually, lead professional development workshops, conduct classroom presentations, and collaborate with undergraduate programs and concentrations to ensure students are career-ready. Reporting to the Associate Director of Undergraduate Professional Development, the CDS will work closely with the Assistant Dean, Corporate Relations Team, and other Career Development Specialists to deliver comprehensive career support. As an active member of the CMC team, this role will also assist with student engagement initiatives, employer events, and other center activities as needed. Please Note: There are two vacancies for this position. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree.  Three to five years in corporate/business experience. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience MBA or master’s degree in a business-related discipline. Two or more years of experience in campus recruiting and/or corporate or business environments. Familiarity with applicant tracking systems and emerging AI job search tools (e.g., Copilot, ChatGPT). Experience or strong interest in using social media platforms such as Canva, Instagram, LinkedIn, and blogs for professional engagement and communication. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Utilize corporate and professional expertise in recruiting, hiring cycles, and timelines to provide career coaching services to undergraduate and graduate students. Provide individual and group career coaching, including résumé and cover letter reviews, mock interviews, LinkedIn optimization, networking strategies, and related services. Offer individual and group career counseling focused on internships, networking strategies, and professional readiness. Work closely with undergraduate professional development classes and their students to support career growth and preparedness. Collaborate with Professional Programs such as DMHP , PPA , PPF , PPM , PPIT , and other specialized honors programs. Partner with select JSOM academic degree programs to develop targeted professional development materials, services, and workshops (e.g., programs for transfer students and Veterans). Collaborate with the JSOM CMC Corporate Relations Team on events and initiatives to develop full-time and internship opportunities for students. Coordinate employer-led events and workshops designed to educate students about various career paths and internship or job opportunities. Create weekly digital content and promotional materials (e.g., flyers in Canva) for the CMC website and social media platforms to promote employer events and professional development opportunities. Maintain accurate metrics and reports for student appointments, workshops, classroom visits, and other events. Develop and maintain programs to collect and analyze internship data for freshmen and sophomores. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We offer an employee-friendly work environment with a comprehensive benefit package including: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training Medical insurance – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability Retirement Plan Options Paid time off Paid Holidays All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities , including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31986": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | HVAC Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help HVAC Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S06710P Position Title HVAC Technician Functional Title Department Facilities Management Salary Range $55,000 – $62,400 ($26.44 - $30.00/hourly) Depending on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Dallas Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 03/17/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 04/20/2026 Job Summary Performs preventative maintenance on HVAC equipment, this includes changing air filters, greasing, replacement of belts, etc. Installs motors, electronics, thermostats, humidistats, fans, other HVAC components, heating water and hydronics, chilled water controls and automated control systems. Assists with troubleshooting and resolving issues with HVAC equipment. Maintain a flexible work schedule including being on-call. Other duties as assigned. Must be willing to work weekends. This position will be located at our Dallas location: 2126 W Mockingbird Ln Dallas, TX 75235. Minimum Education and Experience High school diploma or GED equivalent and a minimum of one year of heating, ventilation, and air conditioning experience. Also requires some basic electrical and plumbing and Building Automation Systems experience. EPA Universal Certification required and must possess and maintain a valid Texas driver’s license and an acceptable driving record. Preferred Education and Experience Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Repair or replace motors, fans, thermostats, etc. Preventative maintenance on HVAC equipment. Respond to hot/cold calls and other related calls. Other duties as assigned. South Campus is a general maintenance shop so in addition to HVAC work you will be assisting with painting, flooring, plumbing, electrical and move and events plus and other duties as assigned. Must possess and maintain a valid Texas Driver’s License and an acceptable driver rating as established in Policy: UTS157 Section 2.5.4. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work Notice: Work will be performed on site and in-person. May be required to report to on-site work location during campus closure. May be required to report to on-site work location during inclement weather. Position will work at our Dallas location: 2126 W Mockingbird Ln Dallas, TX 75235 What we have to offer: We offer an employee-friendly work environment with a comprehensive benefit package including: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training Medical insurance – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability Retirement Plan Options Paid time off Paid Holidays All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. About UT Dallas The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. A collection of people, ideas and perspectives is crucial to our vision and mission. UT Dallas is a place where members of the community are welcomed, treated fairly, and encouraged to their pursuit of excellence. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32504": {
      "title": "Media Technology Specialist II",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Media Technology Specialist II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Media Technology Specialist II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Internal candidates will be given priority. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07198P Position Title Media Technology Specialist II Functional Title Media Technology Specialist II Department Educational Technology Services Salary Range $43,000.00 (DOQ) Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 08/17/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Job Summary This position supports the preparation, setup, operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and continued advancement of the university’s immersive projection classroom and its Pixera-based visualization environment. Working closely with the lead technician assigned to the immersive classroom, this position assists with classroom operations, preventative maintenance, technical support, and instructional activities while developing expertise in immersive visualization technologies and advanced audiovisual systems. The position assists in diagnosing and resolving technical issues, performs preventative maintenance, and helps ensure the reliable operation of the immersive classroom while supporting courses utilizing the immersive projection system. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and the lead technician assigned to the immersive classroom, this position provides technical support, production assistance, and classroom operational support while gaining experience with the design, implementation, and delivery of immersive instructional technologies. Under direct to general supervision provide faculty, staff and students with technical assistance, support, and policy and procedure orientation on media equipment capabilities and operations. Minimum Education and Experience High school graduate or equivalent. A minimum of one year of experience in media technology service, preferably in an education environment. Preferred Education and Experience •Demonstrated aptitude and willingness to learn new software applications, media server technologies, and emerging audiovisual systems. •Experience with Pixera media server software is preferred. •Experience with comparable professional media server platforms (such as Disguise, Watchout, Resolume, Hippotizer, Ventuz, or similar immersive display systems). •Experience supporting advanced projection, immersive visualization, or classroom audiovisual systems. •Experience supporting instructional technology or higher education audiovisual environments is preferred. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities •Configure, operate, troubleshoot, and maintain Pixera media server software and associated projection, playback, control, and visualization systems. •Diagnose and resolve software, hardware, networking, and system integration issues involving immersive multi-projection environments. •Perform software updates, equipment testing, preventative maintenance, and system calibration under established procedures. •Work closely with the lead technician to maintain the daily operation and reliability of the immersive projection classroom. •Support faculty utilizing Pixera and immersive visualization technologies by assisting with classroom operation and the implementation of instructional content. •Provide technical assistance and user instruction to faculty, staff, and students on the operation of multimedia equipment, Pixera software, and immersive classroom technologies. •Follow established operational procedures while assisting in maintaining technical documentation and preventative maintenance records. •Install, configure, update, and maintain operating systems, software applications, and media server software supporting classroom and immersive visualization technologies. •Assist in evaluating and implementing new software features, workflows, and emerging technologies that enhance the immersive teaching and learning environment. •Communicate professionally with faculty, staff, students, vendors, and other university departments regarding technical support, classroom operations, and project activities. •Set up and provide technical support for university events as assigned. •Develop proficiency with Pixera media server software and immersive classroom technologies through hands-on operation, training, and collaboration with the lead technician and Media Services staff. •Participate in ongoing professional development in Pixera, Crestron, Dante, projection systems, media servers, audiovisual networking, and emerging classroom technologies. Physical Demands and Working Conditions •Ability to stand, walk, push or pull equipment on carts weighing up to 70 lbs. •Must be able to bend, stoop, reach, climb ladders, and replace equipment at ceiling level. •Able to work evenings, weekends, or other hours as required. •Remote work is not available for this position. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information THIS IS A NIGHT SHIFT POSITION . A remote work schedule is not available for this position. Will work evenings. May work weekends or other hours as required. The performance of these essential functions requires that the incumbent must be able to stand, walk, push, or pull equipment on cart with wheels, weighing up to 70 lbs., inside or between buildings; must be able to bend, stoop, reach and climb ladders, stretch to reach equipment, and replace equipment at ceiling level. Special Instructions Summary Internal candidates will be given priority. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32343": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Outreach and Recruitment",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Senior Manager, Outreach and Recruitment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Manager, Outreach and Recruitment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested applicants must apply through Safeguard Global. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S06932P Position Title Senior Manager, Outreach and Recruitment Functional Title Department International Center Salary Range Negotiable Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location International Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date Job Summary The Senior Manager for the UT Dallas Latin America Office serves as the university’s primary representative in the region, responsible for advancing institutional partnerships, supporting strategic international enrollment initiatives, and enhancing student engagement across Latin America. This role is designed for an experienced higher education professional with direct experience working with universities in the United States or with institutions that have strong knowledge of the U.S. higher education system. The Senior Manager engages prospective students, families, secondary schools, universities, counselors, and other educational partners to support UT Dallas’s international enrollment and expansion efforts. Working closely with UT Dallas admissions, academic units, and International Center staff, the role advances enrollment strategy and institutional priorities, represents the university at targeted events, and contributes to the development of institutional partnerships. A key responsibility of this position is to support enrollment yield through sustained engagement with admitted students. This includes responding to inquiries, facilitating pre-arrival advising and communications, and supporting events and initiatives that help students successfully transition from admission to enrollment The Senior Manager will also strengthen relationships with UT Dallas alumni in the region and identify opportunities for alumni engagement in student outreach and recruitment activities. Regular visits to the UT Dallas campus are expected to maintain a strong understanding of institutional priorities, academic offerings, and the student experience. Given the independent nature of this role, the successful candidate will demonstrate strong professional judgment, self-direction, and the ability to manage relationships, events, and communications with minimal day-to-day supervision. This role requires confidence in representing UT Dallas publicly and the ability to build long-term relationships that advance the university’s visibility, enrollment, and student success in Latin America. This full-time position is based in Mexico City, Mexico, via contract with Safeguard Global, and includes regional and international travel. Responsibilities also include office and project management, periodic facilitation of seminars and workshops, and presentations at conferences and programs. Minimum Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Six (6) years of experience in higher education admissions, international recruitment, or university partnership development (with direct experience in student lifecycle support from prospect status through enrollment and transition). Demonstrated experience working with an accredited college/university (not exclusively through third-party recruitment agencies) One (1) year of office management experience. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in a relevant field, plus 4 years of academic and administrative experience in higher education, specifically in traditional university settings, preferably in the United States or Mexico. Experience collaborating with university admissions, academic departments, or international offices Experience developing or managing institutional partnerships (e.g., articulation or dual degree agreements, exchange programs, sponsored cohorts) Experience studying, living, and/or working internationally. Experience in an outreach role, as the main representative/point of contact to external audiences, ability to demonstrate judgment, and be comfortable in a public-facing role. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience with office and project management. Contract management experience. Responsible, self-disciplined, and capable of working independently. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Broad knowledge of Microsoft Office programs and social media platforms. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, access, and inclusion. Knowledge of UT Dallas through previous direct experience (as a student, alums, faculty, or UT Dallas community member). Ability to represent UT Dallas through Safeguard Global in a professional and ethical manner. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Institutional Partnership Development Identify, develop, and manage relationships with universities, government bodies, and educational organizations Support development of academic collaborations and partnerships (e.g., articulation and dual degree agreements, pathway partnerships, exchange programs, research connections) Collaborate closely with UT Dallas admissions, academic units, and international programs to ensure alignment with institutional priorities Student Engagement and Enrollment Strategy Engage academic stakeholders, school counselors, and university partners to advance UT Dallas enrollment and partnership goals. Support and coordinate regional enrollment and recruitment initiatives in alignment with UT Dallas admissions policies and student readiness expectations Research and initiate contact with potential feeder schools and universities, develop long-term relationships and partnerships that advance UT Dallas institutional visibility and academic engagement. Seek out and connect with partner campus student groups, campus organizations, and community organizations. Promotion Conduct targeted visits to secondary schools, universities, and government or institutional partners to build sustained academic relationships. Represent UT Dallas by participating selectively at university and college fairs, conferences, symposia, and industry events which increase brand visibility, awareness, and impact Track, monitor, and support the production and distribution of outreach materials and information. Ensure correct brand usage and advanced approval of all materials. Serve as Point of Contact Serve as the main point of contact for the Latin America region with UT Dallas alums and organize events that bring prospective students in front of volunteering alums. Develop relationships with prospective students and families, faculty and campus organizations, and alums networks. Maintain contact with current and prospective partner schools and institutions. Institutional Support Represent UT Dallas from a pre-determined office space, and assist in securing and preparing any further space needed for future programming Assist UT-Dallas faculty and administration during pre and post-admission yield events as well as partnership delegation visits. Assist with regular communications to new and existing partners and prospective student audiences. Work on digital outreach efforts. Work with UT Dallas lead-management system Salesforce to maintain lead flow, analyze communication data, and help strategize outreach efforts based on system knowledge. Visit UTD at least once a year to engage with stakeholders and learn about UTD’s culture and best practices. Other duties as assigned. The above description is an overview of the job. It is not intended to be an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities of the job, as duties and responsibilities may change with business needs. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Fully in-person located in Mexico City, Mexico via contract with Safeguard Global. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information This role does not focus on commission-based recruitment or third-party agent representation. Candidates with primarily sales-driven or agency-based recruitment backgrounds along with direct university experience will receive priority consideration. Candidates located in the Mexico City, Mexico region are encouraged to apply. Candidates will be subject to a criminal background check. Special Instructions Summary Interested applicants must apply through Safeguard Global. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32270": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Part-time Lecturer - Visual and Performing Arts Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Part-time Lecturer - Visual and Performing Arts Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F01160P Position Title Part-time Lecturer - Visual and Performing Arts Functional Title Part-time Lecturer - Visual and Performing Arts Department Arts, Humanities, and Technology Salary Range Negotiable Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular part-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 07/06/2026 Posting Close Date 07/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 08/16/2026 Job Summary Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure. Minimum Education and Experience An earned graduate degree appropriate to the academic discipline/topic and a record of productivity and professional achievement. Preferred Education and Experience Earned Master’s degree in chosen field is required. Two years of college level teaching in an institution similar to UT Dallas is preferred. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Prepare and teach undergraduate classes and/or labs; Maintain contact with student population in the classroom and via electronic learning platforms (eLearning); Contribute assessment information and data as requested through the administration and the Assessment Team; Participate in course evaluation surveys. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this employment opportunity? Governmental Agency Job Posting University's Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement in The Chronicle of Higher Education Advertisement in a Publication or Journal in my Academic Discipline Personal Referral Another Website Other * Which most accurately describes your highest earned degree? Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) Doctor of Education (EdD) Other Doctoral Degree (DSci, DAud, MD, etc.) Specialist's Degree (EdS) Professional Degree Juris Doctor Master's Degree Bachelor's Degree Associate's Degree Certificate * In which Academic Discipline is your highest earned degree? (Open Ended Question) In what areas do you hold any additional licenses or certifications valid in the State of Texas? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Relevant URL Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Teaching Evaluations Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
