    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31264": {
      "title": "Temporary-Part-Time Food Services",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Temporary-Part-Time Food Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Temporary-Part-Time Food Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please Note: Work will be performed on-site and in person. person at the Callier Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number W00219P Position Title Temporary-Part-Time Food Services Functional Title Department Callier Ctr Communication Salary Range $17.51 to $19.00, DOQ Pay Basis Hourly Position Status Regular part-time Location Dallas Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 02/10/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 02/23/2026 Job Summary We are seeking a dependable and well‑organized Part‑Time Food Services team member to join the Callier Child Development Program. This role is essential in supporting daily meal preparation and maintaining a clean, safe, and efficient kitchen environment. Key responsibilities include assisting with the preparation of nutritious meals and snacks, upholding high standards of hygiene and cleanliness, and ensuring full compliance with food safety regulations. This temporary, non‑benefits‑eligible position is scheduled for 19.5 hours per week. Minimum Education and Experience High school graduate or equivalent. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Qualifications 1–5 years of experience in food service, preferably in a childcare or school setting ServSafe certification preferred, or willingness to obtain Experience with point‑of‑sale systems and basic computer/data entry skills Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSAs) Strong attention to detail with the ability to maintain accurate records Flexibility and willingness to cross‑train in all areas of food service operations Commitment to providing exceptional customer service with a positive and respectful attitude Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in preparing and serving meals/snacks for children. Follow dietary guidelines and allergy restrictions. Clean and sanitize kitchen surfaces, dishes, and utensils. Ensure proper food storage and labeling. Assist with inventory and supply management. Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor, designee or Director Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Demands and Working Conditions Equipment and Supplies Used: Cleaning supplies and equipment Microwave, dishwasher, knives, and standard kitchen utensils Sanitation and disinfecting supplies Physical Demands The position requires the ability to: Sit, stand, walk, lift up to 40 pounds, stoop, squat, bend, push/pull, hold, reach, twist, and stretch Move quickly in a fast‑paced environment Multi‑task and manage competing priorities Interact effectively with children, colleagues, and parents Demonstrate patience, emotional stability, and a positive attitude Maintain consistent mental alertness and agility throughout the workday Environmental Conditions Employees in this role may be exposed to: Cleaning chemicals and sanitation products Various smells and occasional contact with bodily fluids Illnesses or contagious diseases Hot and cold temperatures, outdoor conditions, and UV/sun exposure Noise, crying, and busy classroom environments Messy supplies, active children, and fluorescent lighting Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Must provide proof of a negative TB test Must successfully pass all required criminal background checks This is a non-benefits eligible position working 19.5 Hours per week Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person. person at the Callier Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Special Instructions Summary Please Note: Work will be performed on-site and in person. person at the Callier Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
