    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32399": {
      "title": "Child Development Associate",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Child Development Associate - Infant/Toddler Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Child Development Associate - Infant/Toddler Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Work will be performed on-site and in person at the Callier Child Development Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07150P Position Title Child Development Associate - Infant/Toddler Functional Title Child Development Associate - Infant/Toddler Department Callier Ctr Communication Salary Range $39,000 - DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Dallas Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 07/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 08/01/2026 Job Summary Looking for a rewarding opportunity to work with children? Join our Callier Center Team! The Callier Center provides a nurturing, learning environment for infants through kindergarten Age. We focus on developing every child’s specific needs, including communication and language skills, physical abilities, emotional and social growth, and cognitive development. Our Program fosters an environment in which children have the opportunity to communicate, play, and develop friendships with other children whose interests, abilities, levels of hearing and methods of communication may be different than their own. Provide assistance in the provision of developmental program activities for young children focusing on the infant/toddler age group by providing care and developmentally appropriate experiences for infant/toddler age children; maintain a safe and appropriate learning environment; work collaboratively with team members in planning and implementing activities; document observations of individual child development; provide daily verbal and written communication to parents. Minimum Education and Experience High school diploma or GED , and a Child Development Associate ( CDA ) credential. If an applicant does not hold a CDA credential, the applicant must have completed 12 college credit hours of early childhood education, child development, or elementary education coursework. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience Three years of experience working with infant-toddler-age children; Associate in Early Childhood and Child Development, knowledge of NAEYC accreditation criteria and/or Program for Infant/Toddler Care ( PITC ) framework. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist with educational activities in an appropriately designed setting for infants and toddlers; assist with planning and implementing child centered learning experiences in a team taught, developmentally appropriate program; participate in mainstreaming activities with special populations as designated; provide informational feedback to parents as requested; other duties as assigned. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Demands: Must be able to Sit, stand, lift (up to 40 pounds), stoop, squat, climb, run, bend, push/pull, hold, reach, twist, turn, walk, stretch, get up/down from the floor and child-sized furniture Provide consistent visual/auditory/proximity supervision of children and the environment Move quickly Multi-task Handle the demands of children, colleagues, and parents Be Patient Have constant mental alertness and agility Have a positive outlook Have emotional stability Environmental Exposure: Chemicals Smells/bodily fluids Illness/contagious disease Hot and cold temperatures/UV/Sun Noise Crying Messy supplies and busy classrooms Florescent lighting Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Must have a negative TB test. Must complete 24 hours of approved training annually. Must have a cleared Texas Child Care Licensing Background Check. A Provisional Background Check will not be accepted. Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person at the Callier Child Development Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. May use: Computer, IPOD , IPad Basic kitchen appliances and utensils Classroom toys and supplies Broom/mop/cleaning supplies What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We offer an employee-friendly work environment with a comprehensive benefits package including: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training Medical insurance – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability Retirement Plan Options Paid time off Paid Holidays All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities , including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Work will be performed on-site and in person at the Callier Child Development Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Describe your specific experience working with infants or toddlers. What was the setting? What were your responsibilities? (Open Ended Question) What does responsive care look like to you when working with infants? (Open Ended Question) How would you describe Primary Care? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Official Transcripts Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32155": {
      "title": "Student Financial Aid Officer II",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Student Financial Aid Officer II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Student Financial Aid Officer II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07104P Position Title Student Financial Aid Officer II Functional Title Department Office of Financial Aid Salary Range Up to $41,000, commensurate with experience Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 06/22/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Job Summary Are you interested in helping students achieve their educational and professional goals? Are you looking for a rewarding opportunity in higher education that provides a hybrid remote work schedule and a comprehensive benefits package including employee tuition assistance? If so, apply now to join our team! The Student Financial Aid Officer II performs a variety of job duties associated with the coordination, awarding, disbursement, and returning of state, federal and institutional financial aid assistance programs as part of the Office of Financial Aid Counseling and Customer Service Team. This position advises students and families about financial aid processes and requirements, collaborates with other University departments to promote a positive student experience, and works with other Office of Financial Aid teams to ensure efficient and accurate processing of financial aid. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and one year of work experience in Financial Aid or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide information to students regarding federal, state, and institutional financial aid program requirements and procedures; advise parents and students about availability of financial aid, the application process, and rights and responsibilities related to student aid. Accept and process financial aid applications and forms from students, reviewing for completeness and accuracy; communicate with students regarding status of financial aid applications and pending supporting documentation. Keep abreast of federal, state, institutional, and office policies to best advise students of eligibility, verification, and appeal requirements and status; serve as point of contact for complicated/involved issues between processing or technical support and the student (or parent, if applicable). Serve as point of contact for other UT Dallas departments (e.g. Admissions, Bursar, Advising, Veterans Center) regarding financial aid questions and/or issues. Assist students/parents in locating UT Dallas resources (e.g. academic advising, student affairs services, student and academic records services, student finance services) as well as external resources (e.g. NSLDS , loan servicers). Advise students on loan requirements such as entrance and exit counseling, repayment options, and overall debt. Demonstrate integrity and ethical behavior in working with confidential information and maintain a high level of confidentiality. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Requires the ability to sit or stand at will for extended periods throughout the workday; Requires the ability to perform frequent to constant repetitive keyboarding functions to complete work tasks Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information The successful candidate must be eligible to award Title IV student aid. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Strong customer service and support skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills, active listening skills, and interpersonal skills Ability to interpret, apply, and comply with policies and regulations Ability to work effectively both individually and as part of a team Remote Work Notice Following successful completion of an initial training period, a hybrid work schedule may be available, subject to business needs and departmental approval. Employee must be located within the Dallas/Fort Worth Metroplex area and have the ability to be on campus for work activities as scheduled and/or with 24-hour notice. Completion and approval of a UT Dallas Remote Work Agreement will be required, and use of personal computer, internet, and other standard equipment may be required. Remote work arrangements are subject to regular review and re-approval and may be cancelled. About UT Dallas The University of Texas at Dallas is a top public research university committed to admitting, enrolling, and graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. A variety of people, ideas, backgrounds, and perspectives is crucial to achieving our vision and mission. What We Offer UT Dallas aims to attract and retain talented staff and faculty to support the University’s students and mission. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including: Medical with prescription drug coverage (100% paid for full-time employees) , dental, and, vision insurance plans Life, AD&D, and disability insurance plans Flexible Spending Accounts Paid time off and holidays Retirement plans Employee tuition assistance Professional development and training opportunities Employee wellness and employee assistance programs Employee resource groups and much more! Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32562": {
      "title": "Tax Accountant",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Tax Accountant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Tax Accountant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07088P Position Title Tax Accountant Functional Title Department Payroll Salary Range $65,000 - $70,000, Depending on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 09/28/2026 Job Summary The Tax Accountant reports to the Tax Compliance Manager and is responsible for the analysis, record keeping, payments, and reporting functions related to federal and state tax compliance. Responsibilities also include pension fund reconciliation and reporting, the completion of an annual UBIT analysis and private use survey, and communicating with tax authorities and individuals. Performs reconciliation and reclassification of payroll tax, benefits and pension liability accounts. The Tax Accountant analyzes and ensures the timely and accurate completion of tax related documentation and ensures full integration of the status determination into procurement and payroll processes according to applicable university, state, and federal standards. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related field 3-5 years experience in accounting principles and practices as they relate to tax accounting, reporting, and compliance 3-5 years experience researching and applying tax guidance and preparing and reviewing tax and/or financial statements. 3-5 years experience with payroll tax reporting 1-3 experience with sales tax and income tax reporting. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Preferred Education and Experience • 3-5 years of experience with the interpretation and application of federal, state, or local tax laws • Experience with PeopleSoft or similar ERP system • Higher education payroll experience Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Determine the federal, state, and local tax liability for all employees and ensure reconciliations and payments are completed by established deadlines • Complete work associated with the review and production of all new hire and year-end tax forms including payroll tax filings • Provide customer service to employees seeking tax related assistance • Research, analyze, and interpret IRS pronouncements, the Internal Revenue Code, and related laws and state regulations as applicable to University operations • Participate in pension fund reporting and payment processes including annual financial report footnote disclosures • Support and initiate process improvement projects related to tax processes and pension fund reporting • Perform reconciliation and reclassification of payroll tax, benefits and pension liability accounts Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. What We Offer: UT Dallas aims to attract and retain talented staff and faculty to support the University’s students and mission. We are an equal opportunity university and offer a comprehensive benefits package, including: Medical with prescription drug coverage (100% paid for full-time employees) , dental, and vision insurance plans Life, AD&D, and disability insurance plans Paid time off (Vacation, Sick and Holidays) Teachers Retirement System of Texas ( TRS ) – Defined benefit pension plan Voluntary retirement plans Longevity pay after 2 years of service Employee tuition assistance Professional development and training opportunities through our BRIGHT Leaders program and other resources Employee wellness and employee assistance programs and much more! Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Tell us about a time you \"bounced back\" to success. What was the situation? How did you turn a problem into success? (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about one of the most difficult problems you have worked on and how you solved it. (Open Ended Question) * What was the toughest job/position you've ever held? Why, and what did you learn from it? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32133": {
      "title": "Application Administrator IV",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Application Administrator IV Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Administrator IV Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07059P Position Title Application Administrator IV Functional Title DCS Support Engineer Department Information Technology-Digital Transformation Salary Range $98,000 - $105,000 Dependent on Qualifications Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 06/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 07/13/2026 Job Summary The Digital Content Services ( DCS ) team supports enterprise content management, workflow automation, and integrated digital business solutions that enable academic and administrative units to modernize operations, improve efficiency, and support strategic institutional initiatives. This position serves as a senior enterprise application administrator and technical lead for Hyland OnBase and associated enterprise content management and workflow automation platforms. The role is responsible for the architectural design, administration, integration, lifecycle management, governance, optimization, and operational support of enterprise applications and related services supporting mission-critical university operations. This position provides technical leadership for enterprise workflow automation, document management, intelligent document processing, and system integration initiatives involving platforms such as PeopleSoft, Salesforce, identity management services, and other university enterprise systems. Responsibilities include designing and supporting complex integrations, establishing technical standards and best practices, leading system upgrades and modernization efforts, troubleshooting complex enterprise application issues, and identifying opportunities to expand enterprise platform capabilities across campus. The position collaborates closely with campus stakeholders, vendors, project teams, and IT leadership to support strategic digital transformation initiatives, improve operational efficiency, and maximize the university’s return on investment in enterprise application platforms. This position also provides mentoring, technical guidance, and knowledge transfer to team members and serves as a senior escalation point for complex enterprise application and integration issues. Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree and seven plus years of relevant experience; or the equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience will be considered. Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in computer science, information systems, or equivalent experience. Five (5)+ years of hands-on experience administering Hyland OnBase in a complex enterprise production environment. Experience supporting enterprise application architecture, lifecycle management, and complex system integrations. Experience supporting enterprise workflow automation and enterprise content management platforms. Experience supporting APIs, web services, and structured data exchange technologies including XML and JSON . Experience with Windows Server, IIS , SQL Server, and enterprise application troubleshooting. Experience working within Incident, Problem, and Change Management processes. Experience supporting enterprise application upgrades, patching, and lifecycle management activities. Hyland OnBase Certified System Administrator. Hyland OnBase Certified Workflow Administrator. Hyland OnBase Certified API Developer. Hyland OnBase Certified WorkView Administrator or Developer. Strong experience administering OnBase in multi-environment enterprise deployments including development, test, and production environments. Experience designing and supporting complex enterprise workflow solutions including life cycles, queues, timers, Unity scripting, and process automation. Experience supporting and troubleshooting enterprise integrations involving OnBase, PeopleSoft, Salesforce, identity management systems, APIs, and related enterprise platforms. Experience with intelligent document processing, OCR , Advanced Capture, or similar automated capture technologies. Experience designing and supporting enterprise workflow automation and document-centric business process solutions. Experience leading enterprise application upgrades, migrations, modernization initiatives, and platform expansion efforts. Experience developing technical standards, governance practices, operational procedures, and support documentation for enterprise applications. Experience mentoring team members and providing technical leadership within enterprise application environments. Experience supporting enterprise applications within a higher education environment. Strong analytical, troubleshooting, organizational, communication, and customer service skills. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Expected areas of expertise and responsibility include the following: Serve as senior enterprise application administrator and technical lead for Hyland OnBase and associated Digital Content Services platforms. Administer, monitor, maintain, patch, upgrade, optimize, and support Hyland OnBase and related enterprise applications and services in on-premise and hybrid environments. Design, support, and maintain enterprise integrations between OnBase and university enterprise systems including PeopleSoft, Salesforce, identity management services, APIs, and other campus solutions. Develop and maintain architectural standards, operational procedures, governance practices, and best practices for enterprise content management and workflow automation platforms. Lead technical planning, coordination, testing, validation, and deployment activities for enterprise platform upgrades, migrations, patches, modernization initiatives, and expansion efforts. Evaluate, design, and implement enterprise workflow automation and intelligent document processing solutions to improve operational efficiency and business process effectiveness. Configure and maintain OnBase document types, keyword types, file formats, security classes, user groups, workflows, WorkView applications, Unity Forms, and system configurations. Administer and support enterprise workflow solutions including life cycles, queues, timers, Unity scripts, workflow actions, and automated document processing. Support and troubleshoot enterprise capture, ingestion, indexing, and automated data extraction processes including OCR , Advanced Capture, import processors, and related technologies. Develop, maintain, and troubleshoot APIs, scripts, integrations, automated processes, and technical solutions supporting enterprise business operations. Troubleshoot and resolve complex enterprise application issues involving workflow processing, integrations, application services, authentication, performance, and data integrity. Monitor and maintain enterprise application services including IIS -hosted applications, Unity Scheduler, Workflow services, integration services, and related infrastructure components. Coordinate with vendors, infrastructure teams, database administrators, developers, security teams, and other technology groups to support enterprise application operations and strategic initiatives. Partner with academic and administrative departments to identify workflow automation opportunities and modernize document-centric business processes. Support strategic initiatives focused on expanding enterprise platform utilization and maximizing return on investment in enterprise content management and workflow automation technologies. Participate in enterprise architecture discussions, roadmap planning, and digital transformation initiatives related to workflow automation, integrations, and enterprise content management services. Establish and maintain technical documentation, operational runbooks, troubleshooting procedures, standards, and knowledge transfer materials. Provide mentoring, technical leadership, training, and guidance to team members, functional users, and stakeholders. Serve as senior escalation point for complex enterprise application, workflow, and integration issues. Participate in Incident, Problem, and Change Management processes in alignment with university operational standards and ITIL practices. Participate in on-call rotation and provide after-hours support for critical enterprise application incidents and maintenance activities. Perform other related duties as assigned. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information On-call availability required for system emergencies, including after hours. Emergency on-call availability may be required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Remote Work Eligibility Statement Hybrid Remote Work Available for Texas Residents Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
