    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32609": {
      "title": "Lab Technician / Research Assistant",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Lab Technician / Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Lab Technician / Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07211P Position Title Lab Technician / Research Assistant Functional Title Lab Technician / Research Assistant Department Neuroscience Salary Range 40,000, DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 09/02/2027 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Job Summary The Department of Neuroscience at UT Dallas has an opening for a Laboratory Technician/Research Assistant to join the Tavares Lab. The lab studies the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying pain, peripheral neuropathies, and neurodegenerative diseases. Our research uses animal models, cell culture, molecular and histological approaches, and transcriptomic analyses to better understand mechanisms of nerve dysfunction and disease. The Laboratory Technician/Research Assistant will provide technical and research support for ongoing laboratory projects, with a primary emphasis on animal studies of pain and peripheral neuropathy. The position will also provide opportunities to contribute to cell culture, tissue processing, microscopy, molecular biology, and transcriptomic studies. Experience working with rodents is preferred. Training will be provided for specialized techniques. This position is particularly well suited for a recent graduate seeking post-baccalaureate research experience before pursuing a PhD or other graduate training. This position may be fully or in part funded by a grant. Continued employment is contingent on the availability of funds and satisfactory performance. Minimum Education and Experience Associate degree with a minimum of two years hands on experience. An equivalent combination of education and experience is acceptable. Preferred Education and Experience Preferred Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree with major coursework in biology, neuroscience, biomedical sciences, or a related field. Previous laboratory research experience is preferred. Prior experience working with rodents, including animal handling, behavioral testing, surgical procedures, or tissue collection. Experience with molecular and cell biology techniques, such as PCR , nucleic acid purification, cell culture, histology, immunohistochemistry, or microscopy. Experience conducting experiments independently. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties & Responsibilities Conduct and assist with animal experiments related to pain and peripheral neuropathy, including rodent handling, behavioral testing, experimental procedures, tissue collection, and sample processing. Assist with cell culture experiments and molecular and cellular assays. Perform tissue processing, histology, immunohistochemistry/immunofluorescence, microscopy, and other laboratory procedures. Contribute to transcriptomic and molecular studies, including preparation and organization of biological samples for RNA sequencing and related analyses. Conduct experiments under the supervision of the PI and provide technical and research support for other laboratory personnel. Carefully document experimental procedures, protocols, animal records, and research results. Troubleshoot technical and experimental problems and summarize and present results to the research team. Help maintain laboratory equipment, protocols, and SOPs. Maintain laboratory inventory and ensure adequate supplies and equipment are available for ongoing research projects. Assist with orders and deliveries as needed. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities (KSA’s) Experience with or willingness to learn rodent handling and animal research procedures. Basic laboratory experience in neuroscience, biology, biomedical sciences, or a related field. Motivation to learn new experimental methods and techniques. Strong attention to detail and ability to carefully document experimental procedures and results. Ability to troubleshoot technical and experimental challenges. Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to work independently after appropriate training and as part of a collaborative research team. Ability to record, organize, and communicate experimental results clearly. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits BCBS PPO Medical Insurance Options – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees AD&D Insurance Dental & Vision Plan Options Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Fertility Benefits Paid time off All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32395": {
      "title": "Child Development Assistant",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Child Development Assistant -  Infant/Toddler &amp; Two&#39;s Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Child Development Assistant -  Infant/Toddler & Two's Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person at the Callier Child Development Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07165P Position Title Child Development Assistant -  Infant/Toddler & Two's Program Functional Title Child Development Assistant -  Infant/Toddler & Two's Programs Department Callier Ctr Communication Salary Range $36,421, DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Dallas Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 07/22/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Job Summary Looking for a rewarding opportunity to work with children? Join our Callier Center Team! The Callier Center provides a nurturing learning environment for infants through kindergarten age. We focus on developing every child’s specific needs, including communication and language skills, physical abilities, emotional and social growth, and cognitive development. Our Program fosters an environment in which children have the opportunity to communicate, play and develop friendships with other children whose interests, abilities, levels of hearing, and methods of communication may be different than their own. This position will assist in the provision of developmental program activities for infants and toddlers. Minimum Education and Experience High School diploma or GED . Preferred Education and Experience Previous child care experience is preferred. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assist with educational activities in an appropriately designed setting for infants and toddlers; assist with planning and implementing child-centered learning experiences in a team-taught, developmentally appropriate program for infants and toddlers; provide informational feedback to parents as requested; other duties as assigned. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Successful candidates will be exposed to the following elements in this position and must possess certain physical and mental capabilities: Physical Demands: Must be able to Sit, stand, lift (up to 40 pounds), stoop, squat, climb, run, bend, push/pull, hold, reach, twist, turn, walk, stretch, get up/down from the floor and child-sized furniture Provide consistent visual/auditory/proximity supervision of children and the environment Move quickly Multi-task Handle the demands of children, colleagues, and parents Be Patient Have constant mental alertness and agility Have a positive outlook Have emotional stability Environmental Exposure: Chemicals Smells/bodily fluids Illness/contagious disease Hot and cold temperatures/UV/Sun Noise Crying Messy supplies and busy classrooms Florescent lighting Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Must have a negative TB test. Must complete 24 hours of approved training annually. Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person at the Callier Child Development Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. May use: Computer, IPOD , IPad Basic kitchen appliances and utensils Classroom toys and supplies Broom/mop/cleaning supplies What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We offer an employee-friendly work environment with a comprehensive benefits package including: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training Medical insurance – including 100% paid employee medical coverage for full-time employees Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability Retirement Plan Options Paid time off Paid Holidays All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities , including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Work Notice: Work will be performed on-site and in person at the Callier Child Development Center in Dallas — 1966 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Describe your specific experience working with infants, toddlers, or preschoolers. What was the setting? What were your responsibilities? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32147": {
      "title": "Maintenance Worker III",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | Maintenance Worker III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Maintenance Worker III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application and resume review will begin once posting has been open for 5 business days. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07100P Position Title Maintenance Worker III Functional Title Maintenance Worker III Department Housing Operations Salary Range $48,000.00 - DOQ Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 06/18/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 07/06/2026 Job Summary Provide skills in the area of plumbing, electrical maintenance/repair, carpentry and/or painting. Minimum Education and Experience High school diploma or GED equivalent; four years experience in general maintenance duties or trade school; licenses as required. Or an equivalent years of education and/or work experience. Must have a valid Texas Driver’s license and a good clean driving record. Preferred Education and Experience A minimum of three or more years in facility maintenance operations or related experience or training in building maintenance and repair of mechanical equipment. Excellent troubleshooting skills. Knowledge of and experience with electrical, plumbing, inventory supervision, general building maintenance, and repair skills. Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Perform assigned day-to-day repairs and emergency maintenance. Work on building equipment systems – replace filters, inspections and preventative maintenance. Assist with the upkeep of grounds and buildings. Assist with installation and modification of building equipment systems. Maintain lighting systems throughout the facility, cleaning fixtures, and replacing bulbs and lamps. Assist with troubleshooting and repairs of buildings and installed systems. Work independently or as a team member. Conduct minor and major repairs of all buildings and equipment. Perform preventative maintenance procedures on buildings and equipment. Respond to emergencies during scheduled work hours and after hours, including weekends, as needed. Work after-hours, weekends, and on-call duties as assigned. Conduct regular inspections to determine areas that need attention and then perform the tasks. Perform additional duties as assigned by the supervisor. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Demands and Working Conditions: Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Must possess at the time of hire and maintain a valid Texas Driver’s license and an acceptable driving record. May be required to report to on-site work location during campus closure. May be required to report to on-site work location during inclement weather. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Work is conducted on-site. The division of student affairs promotes and encourages student engagement and belonging. We accomplish this through in-person interactions with students, therefore remote work for this position is not available. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees Vision Insurance Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid Time off Fertility Benefits About Us UT Dallas is a top public research university located in one of the nation’s fastest-growing metropolitan regions. Our seven schools offer more than 140 undergraduate and graduate programs, plus professional certificates and fast-track programs. Our student body is 31,000 strong, reflecting students from over 100 countries and a multiplicity of identities and experiences. UT Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the global community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. Special Instructions Summary Application and resume review will begin once posting has been open for 5 business days. Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32561": {
      "title": "LARC Technician",
      "description": "University of Texas at Dallas Employment Opportunities | LARC Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help LARC Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S07212P Position Title LARC Technician Functional Title LARC Technician Department Research Operations & Labs Salary Range $36,421 Pay Basis Monthly Position Status Regular full-time Location Richardson Position End Date (if temporary) Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date Job Summary To assist in the maintenance and operation of the animal experimentation/research facilities. Responsible for the performance of routine non-technical tasks. The training schedule for the Animal Technician is M-F, 8am-5pm. Once adequate training is accomplished (a few weeks depending on experience) new technicians are required to work the weekends and take 2 days off during the week. Minimum Education and Experience High school diploma or GED . Preferred Education and Experience Other Qualifications To the extent this position requires the holder to research, work on, or have access to critical infrastructure as defined in Section 117.001(2) of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the critical infrastructure is a minimum qualification to be hired and to continue to be employed in the position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Review, comprehend and comply with all Standard Operating Procedures (SOP’s)and quality assurance standards pertaining to specific area. Monitor daily animal health/welfare while performing daily animal health observations. Perform animal husbandry duties to maintain quality/health of research animals includes daily bottle/cage checks; provide appropriate food/water; cage changing/cleaning. Assist with restraint, handling and manipulation of various animal species as assigned by the on-site supervisor. Dispose of animal carcasses following established procedures. Observe & report problems involving animal care equipment and environmental support systems. Maintain accurate departmental animal housing/support area record keeping. Record animal health concerns per SOP and/or specified protocols. Receive, inspect and put away received incoming animals; ensure and provide for sentinel animals in each rodent housing area. Operate equipment and use supplies according to safety guidelines. Sanitize facilities, animal housing units, and ancillary animal care equipment. Perform general housekeeping and adhere to safety procedures. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Physical Demands and Working Conditions Lifting and reaching above the head, and being able to lift a maximum of 40lbs. Physical Activities Working Conditions Additional Information Remote work is not available for this position. What We Can Offer UT Dallas is an Equal Opportunity Employer with an employee-friendly and supportive work environment. Our comprehensive compensation and benefits package that is effective as of your hire date includes: Competitive Salary Tuition Benefits Internal Training BCBS PPO Medical insurance – 100% paid for full-time employees PPO and DHMO Dental Insurance Plan – PPO plans include ortho benefits Long and short-term disability TRS Retirement Plan – defined benefit plan offering lifetime annuity upon retirement Voluntary Retirement Plan Options – additional savings opportunities with Tax-Sheltered Annuity Plans and Deferred Compensation Plans Dental/Vision/AD&D Paid time off Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break Fertility Benefits All UT Dallas employees have access to various professional development opportunities, including a membership to Academic Impressions, LinkedIn Learning, and UT Dallas Bright Leaders Program. Visit https://hr.utdallas.edu/employees/benefits/ for more information. If you are looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team! Special Instructions Summary Important Message 1) All employees serve as a representative of the University and are expected to display respect, civility, professional courtesy, consideration of others and discretion in all interactions with members of the UT Dallas community and the general public. 2) The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living, and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. UT Dallas does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, national origin, disability, genetic information, or veteran status in its services, programs, activities, employment, and education, including in admission and enrollment. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities. To request reasonable accommodation in the employment application and interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator . For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination policies, contact the Title IX Coordinator . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Veteran Employment Preference - Form DD-214 Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
